"10814","Breakfast Souffle","Great to prepare the night before when you have breakfast guests.","0.0","","80","0","1 1⁄2 lbs    pork sausage | 9 eggs | 1 teaspoon    salt | 3 cups    milk | 3 slices   day old bread, cubed small | 1 1⁄2 cups    cheddar cheese, grated | 1 1⁄2 teaspoons    mustard | 1 (4   ounce) can   mushrooms (pieces and stems) | 1⁄2 cup    onion, chopped fine | 1⁄2 cup    green pepper, chopped fine","Brown sausage meat, crumble and drain. | Beat eggs. | Add milk, salt and mustard. | Add sausage meat and bread. | Add cheese, onion, mushrooms and green pepper. | Pour into a greased 9x13-inch pan and stick in fridge overnight. | In morning bake uncovered for about 1-hour in a 350°F oven.","","One-Dish Meal"
"10820","Hush Puppies","I like to add 1 minced jalapeno for heat-wow!","5.0","20.0","10","1","1 1⁄4 cups    cornmeal | 1⁄2 cup    self rising flour | 1 teaspoon    salt | 2 medium    onions, minced | 1 egg | 1 cup    milk | 5 dashes    Tabasco sauce | 4 cups    vegetable oil","Heat the oil in a skillet to 350-or medium high. | Combine the corn meal, flour, salt and onions-toss well. | Whisk together the egg, milk and tabasco and stir into the cornmeal mixture. | Drop by the tablespoonful into the hot oil. | Fry to golden brown on all sides-remove with slotted spoon and drain on paper towels. | Serve hot.","https://img.sndimg.com/food/image/upload/v1/img/recipes/10/82/0/QXmtwL7XSHyV8jteyfGL_Hush%20Puppies_0281.JPG","Low Protein"
"10823","Honey Dijon Mustard Dressing","Good on salad or for dipping chicken strips! The recipe came from the 'net somewhere. Original instructions called for whisking together ingredients.","4.0","","15","1","3 tablespoons    cider vinegar | 3 tablespoons    honey | 6 tablespoons    mayonnaise | 1 tablespoon    Dijon mustard | 1 tablespoon   minced onion | 1 1⁄2 tablespoons   chopped fresh parsley | 1 pinch    salt | 3⁄4 cup    vegetable oil","Heat vinegar and honey, stirring until honey dissolves. | Cool. | Combine with remaining ingredients in shaker jar. | Shake until completely mixed. | Refrigerate.","https://img.sndimg.com/food/image/upload/v1/img/recipes/10/82/3/pic327JhK.jpg","Salad Dressings"
"10826","Monica's Peanut Butter Bread","My son loves peanut butter and this is delicious for breakfast and dessert.","0.0","1.0","58","0","2 cups    all-purpose flour | 1⁄3 cup    sugar | 2 teaspoons    baking powder | 1 teaspoon    salt | 1 egg | 1 cup    milk | 3⁄4 cup    peanut butter","Combine the first four ingredients in a large mixing bowl. | Add egg, milk and peanut butter. | Stir the mixture until the ingredients are combined. | Spoon into a greased 8 in x 4 in x 2 in loaf pan. | Bake in a 350F degrees  for 50-60 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. | Cool for 10-15 minutes in the pan before moving to a wire rack.","","Breads"
