"10834","Yukon Sourdough Starter","The longer you keep it, tho more sour it will become!","5.0","1.0","10","7","1 package    dry active yeast | 1 teaspoon    white sugar | 2 cups    potato water, warm | 2 cups    flour | 1 cup    water | 1 cup    flour | 1 teaspoon    sugar","Dissolve yeast and sugar in warm potato water in a stone jar or crock-and make it a really big one or a huge bowl. | Stir in flour, mix well, andplace in a warm spot for 24-36 hours, until mixture is bubbly and sour smelling. | Before using""feed"" the starter with the feed ingredients. | Beat in the starter well and let sit for 8-12 hours, then use. | Always, Always keep at least 1 Tablespoon. | starter for your new batch. | You can keep your starter in the fridge for a few weeks, but set it out the night before you want to use it (feed it first).","","Yeast"
"10835","Picnic; Orange-Apricot-Yogurt Soup","You don't have to go on a picnic to enjoy this light refreshing soup but it does go well outdoors on a sunny day. If you are calorie conscience use non fat yogurt and 2% milk","4.0","2.0","5","1","1 (16   ounce) carton   plain yogurt | 5 ripe apricots, pitted and mashed | 1 cup    milk | 1⁄2 cup    orange juice | 6 slices    oranges (thin slices) | 6 sprigs    mint","Combine the yogurt, apricots, milk& orange juice in a blender (Food Processor) and blend at medium speed for 1 minute. | Refrigerate until well chilled. | Pour into a well chilled thermos. | Carry Orange slices and mint separately. | Float orange& mint on the soup when serving.","","Lunch"
