"36193","Mexican Cornbread Salad","","4.83","8.0","40","13","1 (6   ounce) package   Mexican cornbread mix | 1 (4 1/2  ounce) can  chopped green chilies | 1 dash    sage | 1 (1   ounce) package   ranch dressing mix | 1 (8   ounce) container   sour cream | 1 cup    mayonnaise | 2 (16   ounce) cans   pinto beans, drained | 1 cup    bell pepper | 2 (15   ounce) cans   whole kernel corn, drained | 3 large    tomatoes, chopped | 10 slices    bacon, cooked and crumbled | 1 (8   ounce) package   cheddar cheese | 1 cup    green onion","Prepare cornbread, adding green chilies and sage; COOL. | Combine Ranch dressing mix, sour cream, and mayo;set aside. | Crumble 1/2 cornbread into big bowl. | Top with 1/2 each of: beans, sour creme mixture, green pepper, and next 5 ingredients. | REPEAT LAYERS. | Cover and chill 2 hours. | Serve in lettuce lined bowls, top with tomato wedges.","https://img.sndimg.com/food/image/upload/v1/img/recipes/36/19/3/bv3IgPNTiS6joAtkbKug_IMG_0198.JPG","One-Dish Meal"
"36195","Refrigerator Pickles","Quick and easy Pickle recipe to keep on hand in the refrigerator!","0.0","1.0","10","0","6 cucumbers | 1 cup   sliced onion | 2 cups    sugar | 1 cup    white vinegar | 1 teaspoon    celery seed | 1 teaspoon    salt","Mix well and store in the refrigerator.","","Lunch"
"36200","Faster than Sun Tea","Tastes just like sun-tea, but without all the time. Not bitter like boiled tea.","4.67","8.0","5","6","2 cups    water | 5 tea bags | 1 cup    sugar","Place water and teabags into a microwave safe container. | Microwave on high for 3 and 1/2 to 4 minutes. | Take out tea bags (without squeezing) and pour into clean gallon container. | Add sugar and mix until sugar dissolves. | Fill up container with cold water.","","Beverages"
"36201","Almond Toffee Bars","This is a great recipe. Very easy and nice enough to bake as a gift for the holidays 8)","0.0","","50","0","1⁄2 cup    confectioners' sugar | 1 1⁄2 cups    unsifted flour | 3⁄4 cup    butter, cold | 1 (14   ounce) can   sweetened condensed milk | 1 egg, beaten | 1 teaspoon    almond extract | 6 Skor candy bars, chopped into small pieces | 1 cup    slivered almonds","Preheat oven to 350°. | In medium bowl, combine flour and sugar; cut in margarine until crumbly. | Firmly press onto the bottom of a 13x9-inch baking pan. | Bake 15 minutes. | While baking, in a large bowl, combine condensed milk, egg and almond extract; mix well. | Stir in toffee and almonds. | Spread mixture evenly over crust and bake for 25 minutes, or until golden. | Let cool before cutting into bars.","","Bars"
