"48888","Clark Bar Squares","Chocolate/ peanut butter addicts...beware! You'll be hooked on this one!","5.0","48.0","20","1","1 box    graham cracker, crushed | 2 cups    peanut butter | 1 cup    margarine, melted | 2 1⁄2 cups    powdered sugar | 12 ounces    milk chocolate chips | 1 can    Eagle Brand Condensed Milk","Mix together crumbs, peanut butter, margarine and powdered sugar. | Press firmly into 9x13 pan. | Melt chocolate chips and milk in double boiler. | Spread over bottom layer. | Let set. | Cut into squares.","","Bars"
"48889","Cornstarch Mayonnaise","","0.0","1.0","25","0","1 egg, unbeaten | 2 tablespoons    sugar | 1 1⁄2 teaspoons    salt | 1 teaspoon    dry mustard | 1⁄8 teaspoon    paprika | 1⁄4 cup    fresh lemon juice | 3⁄4 cup    salad oil | 4 tablespoons    cornstarch | 1 cup    water","Place in a bowl the unbeaten egg, sugar, salt, dry mustard, paprika, lemon juice and salad oil Prepare the mayonnaise base by blending together the cornstarch and water in a saucepan Cook over low heat, stirring constantly until boiling. | Boil for 2 minutes, stirring constantly. | Remove from heat and pour this cream over the egg mixture. | Beat with a beater until smooth and creamy. | Keep refrigerated in a closed jar.","","Salad Dressings"
