"53375","Teriyaki Marinade","Perfect marinade for chicken, pork, beef. Great for grilling.","5.0","1.0","5","2","1⁄2 cup    soy sauce | 1⁄8 teaspoon   minced garlic | 2 tablespoons    brown sugar | 2 tablespoons    Worcestershire sauce | 1 tablespoon    lemon juice | 1⁄2 teaspoon    dried ginger","Mix well. | Marinate meat 18-24 hours.","","Asian"
"53378","Mac's Favorite Brownies","These are my dad's favorite brownies. They are very moist, and more ""cake-like"" than most brownies.","0.0","","45","0","3 ounces    chocolate pudding (not instant) | 1 3⁄4 cups    milk | 6 ounces    chocolate chips | 1 chocolate cake mix","Bring milk and pudding mix just to a boil and remove from heat. | Immediately add 6 oz chocolate chips and stir until melted. | Add this to dry chocolate cake mix. | Stir well. | Pour into greased 9x13 pan. | Bake at 350 for 30-35 minutes.","","Bars"
"53381","Black Bottom Cupcakes","Great-tasting, eye-pleasing cupcakes.","4.5","24.0","40","2","2 cups    sugar | 3 cups    flour | 2 cups   cold water | 2⁄3 cup    cocoa | 2⁄3 cup    oil | 1 teaspoon    salt | 2 teaspoons    baking soda | 2 teaspoons    vanilla | 2 teaspoons    vinegar | 8 ounces    cream cheese | 1 unbeaten egg | 1⁄8 teaspoon    salt | 6 ounces    chocolate chips","Mix first group of ingredients well. | Line muffin tin with cupcake papers. | Fill cupcake papers half full. | Blend second group of ingredients. | Place 1 tsp of filling in each cupcake. | Bake at 350 for 25 minutes.","","Dessert"
"53384","Holiday Popcorn","Delicious combination of sweet and salty. Great as a gift in a bag or pretty container.","5.0","9.0","40","1","3 quarts    popped popcorn | 1 cup    dried apricot, cut up | 3⁄4 cup    light corn syrup | 1 tablespoon    vanilla | 1 (6 1/2  ounce) can   nuts | 1⁄2 cup    raisins | 1⁄4 cup   packed light brown sugar | 1⁄4 teaspoon    salt","Toss popcorn, nuts, apricots and raisins. | Blend corn syrup, brown sugar, vanilla and salt. | Pour over popcorn mixture. | Toss until evenly coated. | Put on buttered jelly roll pan. | Bake at 250 for 30 minutes, stirring occasionally.","","Lunch"
